      "writtenOn": "2023-01-13T19:57:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll admit I don\u0027t 100% follow how JNI code is linked.\n\nMy understand is that there are two important targets:\n\n- libservice-connectivity\n  - srcs the JNI files ([here](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Connectivity/service/Android.bp;drc\u003d03a51d567486f94a74b0209d7fb65018358ffbd3;l\u003d106) using [filegroup](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Connectivity/service-t/Sources.bp;drc\u003d6fa4682315f69447736d563e835fac7963e6b042;l\u003d30))\n  - links to libnetworkstats as shared lib\n\n- libnetworkstats\n  - srcs this file (and NetworkTraceHandler)\n  - links to perfetto as a static lib\n  \nI think putting the initialization in the JNI would mean `libservice-connectivity` needs to statically link to Perfetto. Since `libnetworkstats` already needs to statically link it for `NetworkTraceHandler`, I made sure this initialization was in the same shared library to cut down on binary size.\n\nHowever, I now realize there\u0027s no reason to put this in `libnetworkstats/BpfNetworkStats.cpp` rather than `libnetworkstats/NetworkTraceHandler.cpp`, so I\u0027ve moved it.",
